WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.237
An addressing mode explains where an instruction obtains its operand.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:16.100
Immediate data is included in the instruction; register addressing names a register; direct addressing supplies a memory address; register-indirect addressing uses a register pair to identify a location.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.379
The first loads the literal value 25H into A.

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:25.114
The second reads memory location 0025H and loads whatever byte is stored there.

00:00:25.114 --> 00:00:29.850
Without knowing that memory value, you cannot predict A for the second case.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.562
What does M represent in MOV A,M?

00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:38.600
M is the 8085 notation for the memory location pointed to by HL.
